PS5 Pro GPU support (upstream #58 by Borchev, ported to 7.3)

Port of ps5-linux/ps5-linux-patches#58 ("PS5 Pro GPU Support, some SMU backend stuff",
f21f65b) from Linux 7.2.3 to our 7.3 tree. Everything only switches on with the PS5 Pro's
own GPU firmware (amdgpu/viola_*.bin, all 8 files with a valid header, GPU 1002:13da):
 - amdgpu: Viola golden settings (the Cyan Skillfish table split into common, Oberon and
   Viola parts), 64 CUs (max_cu_per_sh = 16, the Pro WGP mask for amdgpu.ps5_cu_unlock),
   firmware selection (amdgpu.ps5_viola_fw), an SMU backend for GPU clock and
   temperature (amdgpu.ps5_smu)
 - mp1: BAPM and active WGPs for the Pro; ps5_thermal: the Pro's temperature sensors
Base PS5s and the BC-250 are unaffected; a Pro without the firmware runs like before.
The table hunk is upstream's post-#58 hunk as is (our 7.3 table is still mainline's);
the SMU condition in amdgpu_discovery.c was ported by hand to 7.3's code.
